<p>Use this dialog box for specifying non-standard paper sizes. To access 
 it, click <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size...</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> menu.<br/>
The graphic illustrates which dimension is width " A ", and which 
 dimension is length " B " in relation to the feed direction.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="unit" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Measurement Unit:</span></p>
<p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">inch</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">mm</span> 
 as the units of measurement.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="size" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Size</span></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="widthlength" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Width:</span></p>
<p>Enter the size of the paper edge (A) that is vertical relative to the 
 feed direction of the printer.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Length:</span></p>
<p>Enter the size of the paper edge (B) that is horizontal relative to 
 the feed direction of the printer.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
